{"tool_name":"alfred","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"alfred","version":"0.6.2","home":"https://github.com/tobiasrausch/alfred","documentation":"https://github.com/tobiasrausch/alfred/blob/v0.6.2/README.md","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"BAM alignment statistics, feature counting and feature annotation","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bty1007","biotools:alfred"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"number":0,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":["make",null,null],"host":["zlib","bzip2","boost-cpp","xz","htslib"],"run":["boost-cpp","htslib"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/tobiasrausch/alfred/archive/v0.6.2.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["alfred --help"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"alfred","identifiers":["biotools:alfred","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bty1007"],"license":"BSD","summary":"BAM alignment statistics, feature counting and feature annotation","home_url":"https://github.com/tobiasrausch/alfred","keywords":["Data Accuracy","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Quality Control","Sequence analysis","Genetics","Bioinformatics","Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":10},"biotools":{"id":"alfred","home":"https://github.com/tobiasrausch/alfred","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"BAM Statistics, Feature Counting and Annotation","addition_date":"2020-04-22T11:39:28Z","last_update_date":"2025-11-05T13:53:16.423152Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Gear Genomics","Rare Disease"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:alfred","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"tobias.rausch@embl.de","name":"Tobias Rausch","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5773-5620","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://www.gear-genomics.com/docs/alfred/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["alirh"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1916"},"format":[{"term":"BAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2572"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"},{"term":"Sequence alignment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0258"},{"term":"Sequence annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0361"},{"term":"Sequence visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0564"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Text data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2526"},"format":[{"term":"Alignment format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1921"},{"term":"JSON","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3464"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"Alfred","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"rausch","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty1007","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2018 The Author(s) 2018. Published by Oxford University Press.Summary: Harmonizing quality control (QC) of large-scale second and third-generation sequencing datasets is key for enabling downstream computational and biological analyses. We present Alfred, an efficient and versatile command-line application that computes multi-sample QC metrics in a read-group aware manner, across a wide variety of sequencing assays and technologies. In addition to standard QC metrics such as GC bias, base composition, insert size and sequencing coverage distributions it supports haplotype-aware and allele-specific feature counting and feature annotation. The versatility of Alfred allows for easy pipeline integration in high-throughput settings, including DNA sequencing facilities and large-scale research initiatives, enabling continuous monitoring of sequence data quality and characteristics across samples. Alfred supports haplo-tagging of BAM/CRAM files to conduct haplotype-resolved analyses in conjunction with a variety of next-generation sequencing based assays. Alfred's companion web application enables interactive exploration of results and comp